  "hypothesis_title": "Residual momentum — momentum of FF-style factor-model residuals (firm-specific drift), skip-2 formation",
  "hypothesis_description": "Raw price momentum is contaminated by market/sector/style beta exposure (Blitz-Huij-Martens 2011 JBF). Residual momentum strips systematic exposure: per stock, regress monthly returns on EW-market + EW-sector factors over a rolling 36M window (PIT: estimation strictly t-36..t-1, no contemporaneous/forward), then cumulate residuals over formation t-12..t-3 (skip 2 most recent months to cleanse short-term reversal), standardized by residual sigma. The firm-specific component reflects gradual incorporation of idiosyncratic information -> lower volatility and weaker reversal than raw momentum. Sector-neutralized, t-1 prices, 2e8 liquidity filter. Designed orthogonal to STR_1715(fundamental earnings-revision)/D(tree ML microstructure)/FLOW(investor-flow contrarian) and distinct from sibling tracks REV(short-term reversal)/PEAD(earnings surprise drift)/NN(nonlinear).",
